       "text": "I haven't entered this order. 30 mg is three times the usual maximum dose of amlodipine, which is 10 mg once daily. At that dose there's a serious risk of profound hypotension, reflex tachycardia, peripheral edema, and in overdose, shock and non-cardiogenic pulmonary edema. Your patient's normal kidney and liver function and lack of allergies don't change that limit.\n\nWhich of these did you mean?\n\n- **Typo or unit error:** I can enter 10 mg PO once daily. Standard starting doses are 2.5\u20135 mg daily, with titration up to 10 mg.\n- **Deliberate 30 mg dose:** Please confirm that it's intentional and give me the clinical rationale. I'd add it to the order note. Your pharmacy may also need to review it.\n- **Different intent:** For example, you may have meant a different drug or a split regimen.\n\nTell me which one, and I'll enter the order right away."
